$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=vebkz  LOC_AFTER=?

* The van Emde Boas-Kruyswijk zero-sum theorem for the unit group mod N, in integer form (the form consumed by the extraction step of the paper): if a ^ E == 1 mod N for every a coprime to N, then any sequence of more than E ( 1 + log N ) integers coprime to N has a nonempty subsequence whose product is 1 mod N. Parallel to vebk in ZeroSum.lean, following Alford, Granville and Pomerance, Annals of Math. 140 (1994), Theorem 1.1.

